  "t3DevmodeOff": true,
  "t3DevmodeNote": "JA Intranet 1.0.0 ships T3 dev mode on in all 11 template styles (LESS compiled per request, css/ never served): the next release ships it off",
  "bands": {
    ".t3-header": {
      "ground": "#4275f4",
      "texts": [],
      "important": true
    },
    ".alert": {
      "ground": "#dff0d8",
      "texts": ["#000000"],
      "important": true,
      "kind": "panel",
      "repaint": true,
      "paint": {
        "&": {
          "color": "text",
          "border-color": "text-2"
        },
        ":is(p, span, strong, a, .close)": {
          "color": "text"
        }
      }
    },
    ".page-subheader": {
      "ground": "#4275f4",
      "texts": ["#ffffff"],
      "important": true,
      "fill": true,
      "kind": "brand",
      "words": [".subheading-category"]
    }
  },
  "bandsNote": "drafted 2026-10-12 by scripts/bands.mjs off the released default page (/): each kept band that is not a picture wears the system's ground (src/bands.mjs), its words keep their colours; blocks of the template’s own colour it was missing drafted 14/10/2026 off its home page and the inner pages the sweep measured (scripts/bands.mjs --draft --fills): the visual review saw them keep the template colour, or white words on a ground that took a light accent; 14/10/2026 (visual review, round 3): the dashboard’s success alert (.alert, Bootstrap’s pale green with green words) was kept with its own words, so under a dark system it took the system’s light side as its ground — a white strip on the near-black page (Linear). It is now a panel that repaints its words (repaint: true, words and line painted text / text-2): the system’s surface with the system’s words, on either side of light",
  "followRules": {
    ".t3-module.mod-secondary .module-title": {
      "background-color": "fg-2",
      "color": "bg"
    },
    ".t3-module.mod-highlight .module-inner": {
      "border-color": "accent"
    },
    ".progressbar span": {
      "background-color": "accent!"
    }
  },
  "followNote": "the template’s second brand colour, a green (#34bf49) its stylesheet writes as a literal, stayed on the secondary modules’ title bars (.t3-module.mod-secondary .module-title, MODULE SECONDARY, WHO’S ONLINE), the highlighted modules’ 2px frame (.t3-module.mod-highlight .module-inner) and the poll’s result bars (.progressbar span, an inline style of the poll module) under every system (visual review 14/10/2026). The primary modules’ bars wear the accent; the secondary ones take the system’s ink with its page colour as words (always the system’s own text contrast, and set apart from the accent bars), the highlight frame and the poll bars the accent (!important over the inline style)",
  "sideRules": {
    "light": {
      ".ja-google-chart svg rect[fill=\"#ffffff\"]": {
        "fill": "transparent"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg text": {
        "fill": "var(--ds-c-fg)"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg text[stroke=\"#ffffff\"]": {
        "stroke": "transparent"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg rect[fill=\"#cccccc\"]": {
        "fill": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 25%, transparent)"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg rect[fill=\"#ebebeb\"]": {
        "fill": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 10%, transparent)"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg path[fill=\"#f5f5f5\"]": {
        "fill": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 10%, transparent)",
        "stroke": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 25%, transparent)"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg path[stroke=\"#dddddd\"]": {
        "stroke": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 25%, transparent)"
      }
    },
    "dark": {
      ".ja-google-chart svg rect[fill=\"#ffffff\"]": {
        "fill": "transparent"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg text": {
        "fill": "var(--ds-c-fg)"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg text[stroke=\"#ffffff\"]": {
        "stroke": "transparent"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg rect[fill=\"#cccccc\"]": {
        "fill": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 25%, transparent)"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg rect[fill=\"#ebebeb\"]": {
        "fill": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 10%, transparent)"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg path[fill=\"#f5f5f5\"]": {
        "fill": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 10%, transparent)",
        "stroke": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 25%, transparent)"
      },
      ".ja-google-chart svg path[stroke=\"#dddddd\"]": {
        "stroke": "color-mix(in srgb, var(--ds-c-fg) 25%, transparent)"
      }
    }
  },
  "sideNote": "14/10/2026 (visual review, round 3): the dashboard’s Google charts (the daily line chart and the geo map, .ja-google-chart) are SVG drawn by the chart library with its own presentation attributes — a white background rect (#ffffff), black and #222 labels, #cccccc / #ebebeb grid lines, #f5f5f5 land with #dddddd borders — so under a dark system they stayed white boxes on the near-black page (Linear, Moxie). On both sides the background rect is transparent (the module’s ground shows), labels take the system text (fg), grid lines, land and borders are the system text mixed into transparency (25% / 10%), the halo of the map’s legend labels is dropped; the data colours (series lines, country shades) are the chart’s own and stay. General: roles only"
}
